{title: 606 - Once to Every Man and Nation}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #606 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 606}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Fm]Once to every [Db]manand [Cm]nation,
[Fm]Comes themoment todecide,
[Bbm]In the [Cm]strife [Fm]of truth with falsehood,
[Bbm]For [Cm]thegood or [Fm]e vil side;
[Ab]Some [Eb/G]great cause, [Fm]God’s [C/E]new [Fm]Messi [Bbm]ah,
[Fm]Offering [Ab/C]each the bloom [Eb]orblight,
[Fm]And the choice goes [Cm]byforever,
[Db]‘Twixt [Eb]that [Fm]darkness [Db]and that [Cm]light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Fm]Then to side with truth [Ab]is [Cm]noble, [Db]when [Bbm]we [Cm]share her wretched crust,
[Bbm]Ere her cause bring [Cm]fame [Fm]and profit, and 'tis prosperous [Cm]to be [Db]just;
[Fm]Then it is [Ab]the brave man chooses while the coward [Eb]stands aside,
[Db]Till the [Eb]multitude [Fm]make [Db]virtue of the faith they had [Cm]denied.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Fm]By the light of burning [Cm]martyrs, [Db]Christ, [Bbm]Thy bleeding [Cm]feet we track,
[Bbm]Toiling up [Cm]new Calv'ries [Fm]ever with the cross [Ab]that [Cm]turns not [Db]back;
[Fm]New occasions [Ab]teach new duties, time makes ancient [Eb]good uncouth,
[Db]They must upward [Eb]still [Fm]and onward, [Db]who would keep abreast [Cm]of truth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Fm]Though the cause of evil [Cm]prosper, [Db]yet [Bbm]the truth [Cm]alone is strong;
[Bbm]Though her portion [Cm]be [Fm]the scaffold, and upon [Ab]the [Cm]throne be [Db]wrong;
[Fm]Yet that scaffold [Ab]sways the future, and behind [Eb]the dim unknown,
[Db]Standeth God [Eb]within [Fm]the shadow, [Db]keeping watch above [Cm]His own.
{end_of_verse}
